\version "2.24.0"
% DEVELOPMENT, bars 99-134.
% c033 (form; Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 125-126, 128, 130, 136): 123-130 theme F2 in G major is no longer a harp solo (the scherzo's development has the harp melody, scherzo 73-80);
% it is passed upward Vc (123) -> Vla (124) -> Cl 1 (126) -> Vln I + Fl 1 (128), each entry on the previous part's last note, with a crescendo by addition into the f cadence at 131; the harp keeps the arpeggios.
% c017: 103-105 the violins enter with motive x half a bar after the low strings' head (stretto), 99-102 keep the two ideas apart first (Adler II PDF 177, 181).
% 99-106: call and response between strings (theme F1's head, F minor 99, B flat minor 103) and woodwinds (motive x, 101, 105).
% 107-110: lament bass F-E-E flat-D-D flat-C (i - V6 - v6 - IV6 - iv6 - V) with 7-6 suspensions in the violins (A&S Unit 31, PDF 551-583).
% 111-114: cadence in F minor; the bass rises F - F sharp (D7, V of G). 115-122: G minor, bassoon 1 solo on theme F2 over pizzicato strings
% (movement I gives the bassoon only short solos, cyclic-notes critic 54). 123-130: G major, theme F2 in the harp alone (its first melodic
% line in the symphony, cyclic-notes 'Still unused'). 131-134: cadence in G (D7-G, f): the development holds one key with its own cadence.

% c034 (orchestration; Adler ch. 15, PDF 154, 156): 123-126 Vln II rest (its held G4 pp lay on and above the violas' F2 G4-F sharp4-E4-D4 in the same colour); it re-enters arco pp at 127 under Cl 1.
% c032 (harmony; A&S Unit 17, PDF 276-277: falling-third root progressions need 10ths or 5-6 above the bass, not 5ths): 111 Ob 1 holds F5 and Cl 1 rises C5-D flat5 (were F-D flat, C-A flat: 8ves and 5ths with the bass F-D flat); 127 Vln II holds G4 (ii7; was E4: G-E over C-A, 5ths with the bass).
